6654"} "Caitlin Leverenz"] ", but Ye was simply too strong for the others and pulled away to win in 2:07.57, with Coutts coming in second in 2:08.15. Leverenz was third, just ahead of Rice, equaling her result in both IMs from the 2010 Pan-Pacs. Ye’s time was an all-time textile best and an Olympic record."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Ye became the sixth swimmer to double in the 200/400 IM, and the fifth in a row. This had been done previously by " [:a {:href "/athletes/51086"} "Claudia Kolb"] " (USA) in 1968, and since 1996, consecutively by " [:a {:href "/athletes/48302"} "Michelle Smith"] " (IRL), " [:a {:href "/athletes/93833"} "Yana Klochkova"] " (UKR) (2000-04), and Rice in 2008. Ye’s two gold medals while still only 16-years-old made her the first to do that since " [:a {:href "/athletes/93722"} "Diana Mocanu"] " (ROU) in 2000."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122325"} "Ye Shiwen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "2:08.90 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "2:08.39 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:07.57 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/115744"} "Alicia Coutts"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "2:10.74 (3 h4)"] [:td {} "2:09.83 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "2:08.15 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126654"} "Caitlin Leverenz"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {: